      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'll try the shell script approach to dump the env on failure. \n\nthe thing is, even with snapshots, it feels like there's something else going on. sometimes the error isn't even related to the environment or the code; it's just like the system behaves differently for no reason, almost like some external force is messing with the execution flow. it's incredibly frustrating. what could cause something that's not a standard race condition or a missing dependency? like, what are the more \"unseen\" possibilities in a high-concurrency environment like ours?",
